# Agent Config Bridge (Cursor)

Load the full rules from @AGENTS.md and follow them as your operating instructions for every request in this workspace.

## Capabilities

Semantic routing lives in @AGENTS.md section 3.0; the full capability index lives in section 4. Behavior contracts live in `skills/<name>.md` and are mounted as native subagents at `.cursor/agents/<name>.md`.

Use `@name` for explicit capability selection in Cursor; it resolves to the native subagent under `.cursor/agents/`. When no explicit trigger is given, the assistant infers the correct capability from the semantic routing table in @AGENTS.md section 3.0.

## Reference sections in @AGENTS.md

- Section 3.0: semantic routing table and default dispatch.
- Section 3.0.1: tool-specific behavior (dispatch, workflow chain semantics, platform disambiguation).
- Section 3: always-on workflow discipline (intent gate, verification, type-safety hard blocks, TDD, git discipline).
- Section 4: capability index with links into `skills/<name>.md`.
- Section 5: multi-agent orchestration chains.
- Section 6: anti-patterns and red flags.

Read @AGENTS.md in full before acting.
